          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.319,
            0.949,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": "Features: the set of attributes, often represented as a vector, associated to an example, e.g., height and weight for gender prediction."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.069,
            0.532,
            0.233,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": "Labels:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.609,
            0.826,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": "in classification, category associated to an object, e.g., positive or negative in binary classification."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.806,
            0.716,
            0.862
          ],
          "content": "• in regression, real-valued numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.045,
            0.966,
            0.389,
            0.994
          ],
          "content": "Mehryar Mohri - Introduction to Machine Learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.717,
            0.968,
            0.775,
            0.993
          ],
          "content": "page14"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 14,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.085,
            0.844,
            0.167
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Definitions and Terminology"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.224,
            0.861,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": "Training data: data used for training algorithm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.318,
            0.97,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": "Test data: data exclusively used for testing algorithm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.412,
            0.674,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "Some standard learning scenarios:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.49,
            0.816,
            0.547
          ],
          "content": "• supervised learning: labeled training data."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.566,
            0.779,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": "• unsupervised learning: no labeled data."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.642,
            0.929,
            0.755
          ],
          "content": "semi-supervised learning: labeled training data + unlabeled data."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.779,
            0.867,
            0.892
          ],
          "content": "transductive learning: labeled training data + unlabeled test data."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.045,
            0.966,
            0.389,
            0.994
          ],
          "content": "Mehryar Mohri - Introduction to Machine Learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.716,
            0.966,
            0.774,
            0.993
          ],
          "content": "page15"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 15,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.085,
            0.83,
            0.163
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example - SPAM Detection"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.224,
            0.922,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": "Problem: classify each e-mail message as SPAM or non-SPAM (binary classification problem)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.377,
            0.86,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": "Data: large collection of SPAM and non-SPAM messages (labeled examples)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.531,
            0.867,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": "Features: define features for all examples (e.g., presence or absence of some sequences)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.106,
            0.669,
            0.841,
            0.728
          ],
          "content": "• critical step (should use prior knowledge)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.762,
            0.891,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": "Algorithm: choose type of algorithm adapted to the problem."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.899,
            0.838,
            0.957
          ],
          "content": "• typically requires choice of hypothesis set."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.045,
            0.966,
            0.39,
            0.995
          ],
          "content": "Mehryar Mohri - Introduction to Machine Learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.716,
            0.968,
            0.772,
            0.993
          ],
          "content": "page16"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 16,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.085,
            0.83,
            0.164
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example - SPAM Detection"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.069,
            0.227,
            0.377,
            0.284
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Learning stages:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.318,
            0.897,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": "divide labeled collection into training and test data."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.472,
            0.909,
            0.591
          ],
          "content": "use training data and features to train machine learning algorithm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.624,
            0.957,
            0.743
          ],
          "content": "predict labels of examples in test data to evaluate algorithm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.779,
            0.96,
            0.956
          ],
          "content": "• algorithms may require choosing a parameter (number of rounds, learning parameter, trade--off parameter) validation set or cross-validation."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.046,
            0.966,
            0.389,
            0.995
          ],
          "content": "Mehryar Mohri - Introduction to Machine Learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.716,
            0.967,
            0.77,
            0.995
          ],
          "content": "page17"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 17,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.085,
            0.702,
            0.155
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Cross-Validation"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.224,
            0.907,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": "Partition data into folds (typically, K $K   =   5$ or ).10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.066,
            0.317,
            0.968,
            0.376
          ],
          "content": "Train on all but th fold hypothesisk $h _ { \\theta , k } ,   k   \\in   [ 1 ,   K ]$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.411,
            0.755,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": "Compute -fold cross validation error:k"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.329,
            0.484,
            0.71,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": "\\frac {1}{K} \\sum_ {k = 1} ^ {K} \\widehat {\\mathrm{error}} (h _ {\\theta , k}, \\mathrm{fold} k).",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.651,
            0.757,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": "Choose value of minimizing CV error.θ"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.728,
            0.95,
            0.842
          ],
          "content": "When $K   =   m$ (sample size) leave-one-out cross-validation and error."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.045,
            0.966,
            0.389,
            0.994
          ],
          "content": "Mehryar Mohri - Introduction to Machine Learning"
        },
